From 9ed799d63c80bfdeeb5661762120009bf96eb3fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pete O_o <pmb@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:26:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MetricReportDefinition: accept PortMetrics properties

MetricReportDefinitions only accept sensor URIs, so the NIC counters
that PortMetrics serves from xyz.openbmc_project.Metric.Value can't be
collected into a report, or streamed from one.

Accept MetricProperties of the form
  /redfish/v1/Chassis/<c>/NetworkAdapters/<n>/Ports/<p>/Metrics#/<property>
and resolve them by walking the same chassis -> adapter -> port ->
measured_by associations the PortMetrics GET handler uses.  The
mapping from Metric.Value object name to PortMetrics property moves
into a table so the GET handler and the resolver share it.

The telemetry service must also be able to read Metric.Value objects
for such a report to be created.

Signed-off-by: Pete O_o <pmb@meta.com>
